      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Interesting idea, here's some insights\n\nas far as i can tell its locked in place while in flying mode to remove unnecessary variables, and allow the controls to be mapped to your joysticks... (you would need 6DoF to achieve what youre trying to do; currently the camera only needs 4 out of those 6 to be mapped to your controllers)\n\nwho wants to have their camera \"rolled\" at anything but 0... ?\n\nwell in your case, you want it rolled at either 90 or 270; so they would need to undo the current \"constraint\" system to allow the camera to be rolled in a vertical orientation....\n\ndon't forget that the camera are taking pictures at a fixed aspect ratio, 16x9 horizontal; and i'm not sure this can be altered in unity without affecting the viewport components too. but at this point i'm speculating and i would let the devs step up and clear out if it's doable or not",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
